    {
      "month": "1993-12",
      "title": "Astronauts repair Hubble",
      "description": "A servicing mission installs corrective optics to improve the telescope’s pictures.",
      "source_ids": ["hubble-repair"]
    }
  ],
  "what_happened_next": {
    "text": "Disney nearly tripled, while Apple lost about half its value. IBM gained, but less than the US share basket. Two companies could work together and still give their shareholders very different results. Spreading money across many businesses avoided depending entirely on either computer company.",
    "source_ids": [
